WEBVTT

01:46.606 --> 01:50.193
Soon? You mean your battle with Baki?

01:54.614 --> 01:56.032
It's not a battle.

01:57.408 --> 01:58.618
It's a father-son fight.

01:59.119 --> 02:02.413
Ogre, don't you realize it?

02:02.997 --> 02:06.793
Baki is trying to get you to cook for him.

02:08.294 --> 02:12.048
I spent a lot of time on the battlefield.
Cooking is no problem.

02:12.132 --> 02:13.299
You can cook?!

02:18.638 --> 02:23.810
Father or son... There isn't any rule
about who does the cooking.

02:23.893 --> 02:27.313
A father and son together
should be congenial.

02:27.897 --> 02:30.316
There's no reason
it shouldn't be enjoyable.

02:30.400 --> 02:31.818
It's just that,

02:31.901 --> 02:35.321
hearing that kind of thing
from you is unusual.

02:36.114 --> 02:39.242
Yujiro, could it be you've...

02:47.083 --> 02:52.839
You weren't about to say "gotten soft,"
were you?

02:53.423 --> 02:56.718
I was going to say
you've gotten even sharper.

03:00.513 --> 03:01.848
<i>Ya know...</i>

03:04.100 --> 03:06.102
<i>I'm getting a premonition.</i>

03:11.816 --> 03:14.068
Though it's a father-son fight,

03:14.152 --> 03:17.071
there's no way to avoid making trouble,
is there?

03:17.572 --> 03:20.491
That's very bold of you.

03:21.868 --> 03:22.994
Me?

03:23.077 --> 03:26.998
Yujiro Hanma is not what you'd call bold.

03:28.666 --> 03:31.085
My dad... He's not bold?

03:33.588 --> 03:37.508
You wouldn't call an earthquake,
thunder or a typhoon bold, would you?

03:38.092 --> 03:42.013
Comparing him to natural forces,
that would make my dad proud.

03:42.597 --> 03:46.017
But you're going to challenge your father,
as soon as tomorrow?

03:46.100 --> 03:49.520
No, no. I'm not going to challenge him.

03:50.605 --> 03:55.026
It's just that, ya know,
there's no telling what my dad will do.

03:55.693 --> 03:58.321
And there are things
that even I won't compromise on.

03:58.863 --> 04:02.784
A father and son don't always
see eye-to-eye on everything.

04:02.867 --> 04:07.538
Baki, to me, the Hanma family
father-son fight is the greatest event,

04:07.622 --> 04:11.542
far more important
than anything else in this world.

04:12.126 --> 04:17.465
Even if I have to mobilize all the police,
riot squads, and the Self Defense Force,

04:17.548 --> 04:19.550
I won't let this fight be stopped.

04:20.134 --> 04:21.094
You're mistaken.

04:22.470 --> 04:25.306
Do you really think
there's an army somewhere

04:25.390 --> 04:27.558
that can stop Yujiro Hanma?

04:29.686 --> 04:30.812
But I'll stop him.

04:32.397 --> 04:34.399
You'll stop him, with your own hands?

04:34.482 --> 04:35.316
RESILIENCE

04:35.400 --> 04:39.737
Yep. I'm his blood relative, after all.

04:42.865 --> 04:46.327
Mitsunari,
I'd like your help when it happens.

04:47.161 --> 04:50.915
Please protect the civilians
so they don't get caught up in it.

04:53.501 --> 04:54.836
Understood.

04:55.420 --> 04:58.131
I will absolutely not allow
this fight to be stopped!

04:58.214 --> 05:00.258
I told you, that's not what I mean.

05:01.676 --> 05:05.305
You're in love? With whom?

05:10.059 --> 05:12.729
My son, Baki.

05:12.812 --> 05:14.480
Really?

05:14.564 --> 05:16.232
I've been waiting for this day.

05:16.983 --> 05:21.404
The seed that I painstakingly
nurtured has grown

05:21.487 --> 05:23.740
and at long last bared its fangs at me.

05:23.823 --> 05:26.492
Oh, that's what you mean.

05:27.076 --> 05:28.244
I noticed...

05:37.670 --> 05:40.089
all I think about is my son.

05:40.923 --> 05:42.759
No matter what I do,

05:42.842 --> 05:45.762
he's always occupying a part of my heart.

05:49.599 --> 05:51.267
You're right about that.

05:51.351 --> 05:53.353
That certainly is love.

05:58.983 --> 06:00.860
There's a dream I often have.

06:00.943 --> 06:01.778
Really?

06:02.403 --> 06:05.782
A dream where I can't lay a finger on him.

06:06.866 --> 06:08.534
You think it'll come true?

06:13.581 --> 06:15.541
No way it'll come true.

06:16.125 --> 06:17.710
That's why it's called a dream.

06:19.045 --> 06:21.047
You sure look happy, Ogre.

06:21.672 --> 06:23.633
I'm a little jealous.

06:27.929 --> 06:29.806
69
I sure wouldn't.

06:31.891 --> 06:33.142
I figured as much.

06:33.226 --> 06:37.313
If Yujiro Hanma is the opponent,
I couldn't do it.

06:37.397 --> 06:40.149
You wouldn't even go
to where the fight is at?

06:41.192 --> 06:45.071
You see, I'm the ultimate embodiment
of self-defense.

06:45.655 --> 06:46.823
That's for sure.

06:47.407 --> 06:48.574
Baki...

06:50.660 --> 06:53.579
See, Baki? It's just not possible.

06:55.706 --> 07:00.586
Look at the stunning skill set
you've mastered.

07:01.462 --> 07:04.590
You should really give up
on this father-son fight.

07:04.674 --> 07:07.093
Yujiro Hanma was once

07:07.176 --> 07:10.596
the target of everyone
who was skilled in martial arts.

07:10.680 --> 07:15.101
But before long,
nobody challenged him anymore.

07:16.686 --> 07:18.729
He'd grown far too strong.

07:18.813 --> 07:21.107
He ceased to even be a target.

07:21.691 --> 07:25.611
There's no shame in running from Yujiro.

07:26.195 --> 07:28.406
Openly run away from him.

07:28.489 --> 07:31.617
There's not a soul who would laugh at you.

07:33.286 --> 07:36.372
Mr. Shibukawa, you are also mistaken.

07:38.207 --> 07:40.960
This tactical idea
of avoiding a fight you cannot win...

07:41.961 --> 07:44.630
It's not a duel. It's not a face-off.

07:45.381 --> 07:49.385
It's not even a comparison
of strength or a match.

07:50.261 --> 07:53.389
It's between father and son,
nothing more and nothing less.

07:53.973 --> 07:56.350
You don't do it
because there's a chance to win.

07:56.851 --> 07:59.145
You don't avoid it because you might lose.

07:59.770 --> 08:03.649
It might never happen,
or it may happen as soon as tomorrow.

08:03.733 --> 08:07.153
In fact, this isn't something you arrange.

08:07.737 --> 08:09.405
Oh, sorry...

08:10.531 --> 08:15.161
Baki, in my own way,

08:15.244 --> 08:18.289
I understand quite well
what I've misunderstood.

08:20.791 --> 08:25.171
<i>Mr. Shibukawa, all the sons in the world</i>

08:26.088 --> 08:28.674
<i>have the right to oppose their fathers.</i>

08:29.425 --> 08:32.637
<i>And it's the duty of their fathers
to accept that.</i>

08:34.096 --> 08:38.976
<i>I believe that's the way
fathers and sons should be.</i>

08:43.564 --> 08:47.193
<i>Not so much a premonition.
More like a certainty.</i>

09:01.040 --> 09:02.458
<i>Yeah, that's good.</i>

09:02.959 --> 09:06.045
<i>Plenty of grated daikon radish
with the grilled fish.</i>

09:06.128 --> 09:07.713
<i>Lightly pickled cucumbers.</i>

09:07.797 --> 09:11.884
<i>Seaweed roots, rice and miso soup.
And a steak in the middle.</i>

09:18.849 --> 09:20.851
<i>He came! I knew it!</i>

09:26.649 --> 09:28.818
<i>Who cares what the reason is.</i>

09:30.278 --> 09:33.948
<i>Just the fact that my dad is here,
that's good enough.</i>

09:35.866 --> 09:37.410
Did something happen here?

09:37.994 --> 09:41.914
My apologies, but I am not permitted
to speak due to my position.

09:42.498 --> 09:43.374
I see.

09:44.750 --> 09:45.918
Let's eat.

09:49.088 --> 09:50.673
<i>Dad bowed?!</i>

09:52.049 --> 09:54.176
<i>He bowed in appreciation of the food?!</i>

09:54.760 --> 09:57.680
<i>I didn't know he did that.</i>

10:01.517 --> 10:06.772
<i>Do I... even know this guy properly?</i>

10:09.358 --> 10:10.693
<i>"Thank you for this food."</i>

10:11.444 --> 10:13.613
<i>What did he bow to anyway?</i>

10:14.780 --> 10:17.867
<i>To his parents? To the living things
that became this food?</i>

10:17.950 --> 10:21.537
<i>To all the people involved in the process?
Or all those things?</i>

10:22.163 --> 10:24.248
<i>Or maybe none of them?</i>

10:26.834 --> 10:31.339
<i>Or me? Don't say he bowed to me?!</i>

10:33.507 --> 10:34.842
No good.

10:37.887 --> 10:40.097
Don't haphazardly stick food
in your mouth.

10:41.515 --> 10:45.603
Be aware of what's in front of you,
of what you're eating.

10:46.187 --> 10:51.108
That is the responsibility, the duty
imposed on those who consume life.

10:52.860 --> 10:53.861
Okay.

10:56.697 --> 10:58.366
<i>What an exemplary thing to say.</i>

10:59.158 --> 11:01.869
<i>There's not even an iota
of room for rebuttal.</i>

11:04.705 --> 11:06.624
<i>I've thought a lot about this guy.</i>

11:07.708 --> 11:09.335
<i>I've hated much about him.</i>

11:09.960 --> 11:12.838
<i>I became strong so I could overcome him.</i>

11:12.922 --> 11:16.258
<i>I have achieved real growth
in my path to know him better.</i>

11:16.967 --> 11:18.469
<i>But look at me now.</i>

11:18.552 --> 11:21.972
<i>Now, after all that,
I'm shocked at myself.</i>

11:23.307 --> 11:26.894
<i>What the heck do I even know
about this guy?</i>

11:30.231 --> 11:33.651
I've been eating a lot
of those seaweed roots lately.

11:35.861 --> 11:37.446
It's good for you.

11:37.530 --> 11:39.907
It comes pre-packaged,
so there's other stuff in it,

11:40.700 --> 11:41.909
but it's good for you.

11:44.495 --> 11:49.417
Preservatives, food coloring,
antiseptics, and various chemicals.

11:50.209 --> 11:51.919
How can they be good for you?

11:52.503 --> 11:55.923
However, only eating healthy foods.

11:56.507 --> 11:58.426
I can't say that's very sound either.

11:59.009 --> 12:01.429
Eat both poison and nutritious food.

12:02.054 --> 12:06.642
Enjoy the taste of both
and transform them into flesh and blood.

12:06.726 --> 12:08.436
That attitude is vital with food.

12:09.770 --> 12:12.523
<i>Holy crap. I think I'm gonna cry.</i>

12:12.606 --> 12:15.443
<i>My dad's educating me properly.</i>

12:16.235 --> 12:19.447
<i>Dang. What wonderful betrayals.</i>

12:20.364 --> 12:23.200
<i>I never knew my dad
held his chopsticks so magnificently.</i>

12:23.784 --> 12:25.953
<i>That he could handle them so beautifully.</i>

12:26.662 --> 12:29.039
<i>All the pieces of etiquette I lack,</i>

12:29.123 --> 12:31.959
<i>my own father mastered them so smartly.</i>

12:34.211 --> 12:38.048
<i>I didn't know
that's how fish should be eaten.</i>

12:39.341 --> 12:40.342
<i>I'm so proud.</i>

12:40.843 --> 12:44.013
<i>This is the first time
I've been so honestly proud of my dad.</i>

12:44.096 --> 12:44.972
<i>That's why...</i>

12:45.848 --> 12:47.308
<i>That's why I wanna say it!</i>

12:48.058 --> 12:51.312
<i>"Dad, can you do the dishes today?"</i>

13:01.322 --> 13:03.741
<i>He's bowing again.</i>

13:04.825 --> 13:06.035
<i>No doubt about it.</i>

13:06.118 --> 13:09.747
<i>Dad expresses gratitude
at the start and end of a meal.</i>

13:10.498 --> 13:12.750
<i>He's got way better manners than I do.</i>

13:14.418 --> 13:15.336
<i>I'm gonna say it.</i>

13:16.086 --> 13:19.089
<i>Not to the strongest being on Earth,
Yujiro Hanma.</i>

13:20.424 --> 13:22.092
<i>To my father, Yujiro Hanma...</i>

13:22.885 --> 13:25.346
<i>No, to my dad.</i>

13:26.096 --> 13:30.601
<i>Right, I'm gonna casually ask my own dad.</i>

13:35.397 --> 13:36.232
Dad.

13:36.315 --> 13:37.274
<i>I said it!</i>

13:38.359 --> 13:39.902
Sorry, but...

13:40.611 --> 13:42.279
<i>There's no reason to be sorry!</i>

13:43.113 --> 13:44.365
...today...

13:44.865 --> 13:46.784
<i>Why the heck not every day?!</i>

13:47.451 --> 13:49.078
...can you do the dishes?

13:49.161 --> 13:50.412
<i>I said it!</i>

13:50.996 --> 13:53.499
I know you're pretty busy yourself, but...

13:54.875 --> 13:56.877
<i>He's not answering. Why's he silent?!</i>

13:57.503 --> 13:58.796
Could you do...

14:02.383 --> 14:05.052
<i>A punch... As punishment?</i>

14:05.678 --> 14:08.639
- Let's rock-paper-scissors for it.
- Huh? Rock...

14:09.640 --> 14:13.561
If you beat me at rock-paper-scissors,
I'll do the dishes.

14:13.644 --> 14:15.604
Oh... Yes sir.

14:16.146 --> 14:17.857
<i>Why are you being so polite?!</i>

14:21.318 --> 14:23.404
One, two, three.

14:26.156 --> 14:27.616
<i>I won!</i>

14:27.700 --> 14:30.077
<i>I get to watch my dad wash dishes!</i>

14:34.290 --> 14:37.543
Huh? Uh, Dad...

14:52.308 --> 14:53.183
See?

14:53.851 --> 14:55.060
Seriously?

14:56.562 --> 14:58.105
Remember this.

14:58.188 --> 15:01.942
There are scissors in this world
that can cut through rock.

15:05.362 --> 15:08.324
"See?" What total bullshit!

15:14.997 --> 15:16.123
Everything's normal.

15:16.707 --> 15:19.043
Yeah, I guess you could call it normal.

15:22.880 --> 15:24.006
No way!

15:26.884 --> 15:27.760
You bastards.

15:29.345 --> 15:32.264
What're you doing loitering
around someone's house?

15:40.356 --> 15:43.275
Hey, you gonna stop me?

15:57.665 --> 15:59.041
<i>Unbelievable.</i>

15:59.959 --> 16:02.753
I feel bad that you're always
the one inviting me.

16:03.462 --> 16:07.049
I'd like to invite you out tomorrow.
Leave your schedule open.

16:10.344 --> 16:12.346
<i>What should I wear?</i>

16:18.268 --> 16:19.311
<i>Aw man...</i>

16:21.271 --> 16:24.692
This outfit's not gonna work.

16:25.567 --> 16:28.195
In fact, this is absolutely ridiculous.

16:28.904 --> 16:30.030
All of it.

16:31.615 --> 16:34.201
We've been expecting you, Mr. Hanma.

16:34.827 --> 16:37.329
We have a private room ready for you.

16:37.413 --> 16:38.330
This way, please.

16:43.794 --> 16:46.714
<i>Is that the price for just one serving?</i>

16:50.300 --> 16:52.219
<i>The whole wall is a window.</i>

16:53.387 --> 16:55.723
Does it please you?

16:55.806 --> 16:58.225
Does my father often use this room?

16:58.809 --> 17:01.020
Yes. He comes here quite often.

17:01.520 --> 17:03.731
What kinds of things does he eat here?

17:04.314 --> 17:06.483
He eats a lot of everything.

17:07.151 --> 17:09.820
But rather than domestic animals
such as beef and chicken,

17:09.903 --> 17:14.491
he has a preference for game meat,
like venison, wild duck, boar and...

17:15.367 --> 17:17.995
Mr. Hanma! When did you arrive?

17:18.662 --> 17:19.747
Dad...

17:21.665 --> 17:24.877
Manager, that's personal information.

17:25.419 --> 17:28.255
Dear me! I meant nothing of it.

17:28.839 --> 17:30.758
Dad's wearing a suit jacket?

17:30.841 --> 17:34.136
I've heard that he is your beloved son.

17:34.219 --> 17:36.513
I supposed that since you're related...

17:36.597 --> 17:39.016
And just look at my son's
shameful appearance.

17:39.600 --> 17:41.351
<i>There he goes! I knew it.</i>

17:41.435 --> 17:42.519
I'm sorry.

17:42.603 --> 17:45.272
If you're going to
a metropolitan hotel to dine

17:45.355 --> 17:49.234
you must wear a suit jacket,
no matter where the cuisine is from.

17:49.318 --> 17:52.279
How can a proper 18-year-old man
not know that?

17:53.030 --> 17:56.283
Sorry. Nobody ever taught me that.

17:56.366 --> 17:58.285
Is that a snide remark?

18:04.083 --> 18:05.542
You better believe it.

18:07.377 --> 18:10.464
Proper greetings. Proper speech.

18:10.547 --> 18:14.301
Proper dress.
Proper communication. Proper manners.

18:15.385 --> 18:17.805
I've not once been taught
any of those things.

18:19.264 --> 18:22.059
Grow strong. Be strong.

18:22.726 --> 18:25.145
That's the only message
that my father, Yujiro Hanma,

18:25.229 --> 18:29.066
constantly sent to his son, Baki.

18:29.942 --> 18:31.318
I obeyed that.

18:32.903 --> 18:36.323
I'm strong. In that one thing,
I did just as you taught me.

18:37.199 --> 18:40.077
Go ahead and test me.
You can even do it here.

18:40.661 --> 18:42.079
Mr... Mr. Hanma...

18:46.250 --> 18:47.334
Have a seat.

18:52.172 --> 18:55.926
So, would you like
a light beverage before dinner?

18:56.009 --> 18:56.844
Yes.

18:57.427 --> 18:59.096
Fresh orange juice, please.

18:59.680 --> 19:02.182
A dry sherry in a large glass, please.

19:10.190 --> 19:12.109
This is a typical apéritif.

19:13.026 --> 19:13.861
Try some.

19:18.740 --> 19:20.284
That's good.

19:20.367 --> 19:21.201
Yes.

19:22.035 --> 19:26.123
<i>And that's how
our father-son repast kicked off.</i>

19:26.707 --> 19:27.958
<i>It was so unreal.</i>

19:28.500 --> 19:30.127
<i>Dining out with my dad...</i>

19:30.878 --> 19:32.462
<i>The experience was all too new.</i>

19:32.963 --> 19:35.674
Allow me to tell you about the appetizer.

19:36.258 --> 19:39.303
This is ground black truffles
seasoned with rock salt

19:39.386 --> 19:41.388
and flavored with a paste

19:41.471 --> 19:43.056
made from whole olives.

19:43.599 --> 19:46.393
It's combined with strained tofu
and fresh cream

19:46.476 --> 19:47.895
to suit the Japanese palate.

19:47.978 --> 19:50.147
It's one of the chef's recommendations.

19:50.230 --> 19:51.356
Please, enjoy.

19:52.524 --> 19:54.318
Use the utensils from the outside.

19:55.027 --> 19:56.904
For this dish, a spoon is best.

19:58.071 --> 19:58.906
Okay.

20:03.410 --> 20:04.411
<i>This is great!</i>

20:04.995 --> 20:07.414
This is amazing. It's delicious.

20:08.999 --> 20:10.667
<i>So that's how you place the spoon.</i>

20:13.462 --> 20:17.174
<i>I can understand a meat,
vegetable, or seafood soup,</i>

20:17.758 --> 20:19.676
<i>but sea turtle soup?</i>

20:23.013 --> 20:24.681
<i>Ah, that's delicious.</i>

20:25.557 --> 20:26.683
<i>It goes without saying</i>

20:26.767 --> 20:29.728
<i>that during our father-son repast,
time passed quietly.</i>

20:31.063 --> 20:34.024
<i>We were simply eating out,
so it's only natural.</i>

20:36.276 --> 20:39.696
If you would like,
how about something sweet?

20:40.280 --> 20:41.531
No thanks.

20:41.615 --> 20:43.951
I'll take an espresso in a large mug.

20:44.534 --> 20:45.619
The same for me.

20:45.702 --> 20:46.828
Certainly.

20:48.080 --> 20:50.916
<i>Even here, my dad's behavior was amazing.</i>

20:51.667 --> 20:55.462
<i>I was genuinely proud to see
how accustomed he was to places like this.</i>

21:00.300 --> 21:01.510
<i>It's bitter.</i>

21:01.593 --> 21:05.973
<i>Just why does espresso coffee
have to be this bitter?</i>

21:07.432 --> 21:11.478
<i>It was bitter, and then...
an even more bitter conversation began.</i>

21:12.187 --> 21:14.231
Why are you asking that now?

21:15.941 --> 21:16.817
"Why"?

21:17.818 --> 21:20.112
Because I really want to know.

21:21.071 --> 21:22.489
Is it really so strange?

21:22.572 --> 21:25.742
Is it so strange to want to know
why my father killed my mother?

21:26.451 --> 21:28.245
I've never once asked before.

21:28.328 --> 21:31.748
Why? Why did you kill Mom, Dad?

21:34.084 --> 21:36.503
Certain lines should not be crossed

21:36.586 --> 21:39.006
with the comprehension level
of a bratty child.

21:39.089 --> 21:41.258
Know your place!

21:42.092 --> 21:44.511
As her son, it's my right to know.

21:52.602 --> 21:57.774
So, Dad, what do I gotta do
to get you to tell me?

22:01.111 --> 22:02.529
So, Dad...

22:04.740 --> 22:06.033
Excuse me.

22:09.453 --> 22:11.038
Is this what I have to do?

22:11.121 --> 22:13.290
Why... you...

22:13.373 --> 22:15.042
Or maybe

22:16.418 --> 22:17.377
like this!
